{
  "description" : "The receiver gate (flowcatalyst contract section 4, 'Signature check', and 4a slice 4). Setup per case: signing secret (null = none configured), optional bearer token, requireSignature, and the clock 'now'. The signature is lowercase hex HMAC-SHA256, keyed with the secret as UTF-8, over the raw X-FlowCatalyst-Timestamp header string followed by the raw body bytes; the timestamp is ISO-8601 (Instant) or ASCII-digit Unix seconds, at most 64 characters, compared in whole seconds: refused when older than now-300 or later than now+60. A signature that is not 64 characters is refused before hashing; upper-case hex is lower-cased first and accepted. Headers are an ordered list of [name, value] (names compare case-insensitively) so one can be sent twice. expect.accepted is the gate's answer; when refused, status is 401 and the envelope is {error: UNAUTHENTICATED, message: 'the delivery could not be authenticated', details: {reason}}; reason is one of the codes in expect. hmacVectors are the signature function alone.",
